```

The site is available at <http://localhost:8000>. Stop the local server with
Ctrl-C.{% if database != "sqlite3" %} Run `make stop` when you also want to stop
the database container.{% endif %} Run `make help` to see all available
development commands.

## Docker setup

{% if database == "sqlite3" %}Copy the example environment file to change the forwarded web port, then start
the complete development environment:
{% else %}Copy the example environment file to change credentials or forwarded ports, then
start the complete development environment:
{% endif %}

```shell
cp .env.example .env
make docker
```

`make docker` refreshes the floating `python:{{ python_version }}-slim`
development image before starting the services. This keeps Docker on the same
Python major/minor line while allowing patch updates.

Compose {% if database != "sqlite3" %}waits for {{ database_name }}, {% endif %}applies migrations and serves
Wagtail at <http://localhost:8000>. Create an administrator in another terminal:

```shell
docker compose exec web python manage.py createsuperuser
```

Stop the services with `make stop`.{% if database != "sqlite3" %} Run
`docker compose down --volumes` to also delete the local database data.{% endif %}
{% if database == "mysql" %}

> [!NOTE]
> Django warns that MySQL cannot enforce Wagtail's conditional `WorkflowState`
> uniqueness constraint. This is a database limitation rather than a setup error.
{% endif %}

